('values:lms_lesson:352','O:31:\"Drupal\\lms_lesson\\Entity\\Lesson\":30:{s:15:\"\0*\0entityTypeId\";s:10:\"lms_lesson\";s:15:\"\0*\0enforceIsNew\";N;s:12:\"\0*\0typedData\";N;s:17:\"\0*\0originalEntity\";N;s:16:\"\0*\0cacheContexts\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0cacheTags\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0cacheMaxAge\";i:-1;s:14:\"\0*\0_serviceIds\";a:0:{}s:18:\"\0*\0_entityStorages\";a:0:{}s:9:\"\0*\0values\";a:23:{s:2:\"id\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:3:\"352\";}s:4:\"uuid\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:36:\"bef4eaa7-bdaa-466f-b8d0-0b66b5f136a9\";}s:8:\"langcode\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:2:\"en\";}s:4:\"name\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:43:\"Natural Language Processing (NLP) Explained\";}s:13:\"field_content\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";a:2:{s:5:\"value\";s:1004:\"<h2>Introduction to NLP</h2><p>Natural Language Processing (NLP) is a field of AI that focuses on the interaction between computers and humans using natural language. It enables machines to read, understand, and generate human language.</p><h3>How NLP Works</h3><p>NLP involves several steps: tokenization, parsing, semantic understanding, and sentiment analysis. These steps help in extracting meaningful information from text.</p><h3>Applications of NLP</h3><p>NLP is used in various applications such as chatbots, sentiment analysis, translation services, and voice-activated assistants.</p><ul><li>Chatbots: Provide customer support and enhance user interaction.</li><li>Sentiment Analysis: Understand customer opinions and feedback.</li><li>Translation Services: Break language barriers in global communication.</li></ul><h3>Challenges in NLP</h3><p>Despite its advancements, NLP faces challenges like ambiguity in language, cultural differences, and the need for large datasets to train models.</p>\";s:6:\"format\";s:9:\"full_html\";}}s:10:\"field_type\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:4:\"text\";}s:15:\"field_video_url\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:119:\"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Natural+Language+Processing+basics+tutorial%2C+NLP+explain