('values:lms_lesson:496','O:31:\"Drupal\\lms_lesson\\Entity\\Lesson\":30:{s:15:\"\0*\0entityTypeId\";s:10:\"lms_lesson\";s:15:\"\0*\0enforceIsNew\";N;s:12:\"\0*\0typedData\";N;s:17:\"\0*\0originalEntity\";N;s:16:\"\0*\0cacheContexts\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0cacheTags\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0cacheMaxAge\";i:-1;s:14:\"\0*\0_serviceIds\";a:0:{}s:18:\"\0*\0_entityStorages\";a:0:{}s:9:\"\0*\0values\";a:23:{s:2:\"id\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:3:\"496\";}s:4:\"uuid\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:36:\"e31cfdbd-6869-4a4d-8c4f-8cdcef43fc93\";}s:8:\"langcode\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:2:\"en\";}s:4:\"name\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:53:\"Orchestration Basics with Kubernetes for ML Workloads\";}s:13:\"field_content\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";a:2:{s:5:\"value\";s:1646:\"<h2>Introduction to Kubernetes</h2><p>Kubernetes is an open-source platform designed to automate the deployment, scaling, and operation of application containers. It is widely used for orchestrating machine learning workloads due to its ability to manage complex applications.</p><h3>Why Use Kubernetes for ML?</h3><p>Machine learning models often require the management of multiple components such as data preprocessing, model training, and deployment. Kubernetes provides a robust framework to handle these components efficiently.</p><ul><li>Scalability: Automatically adjust resources based on workload demand.</li><li>Portability: Run workloads on any infrastructure, whether on-premises or in the cloud.</li><li>Resilience: Quickly recover from failures and ensure high availability.</li></ul><h3>Key Features</h3><p>Kubernetes offers several features that are particularly beneficial for ML workloads:</p><ol><li><strong>Container Orchestration:</strong> Simplifies the management of containerized applications.</li><li><strong>Resource Management:</strong> Allocates resources dynamically, ensuring optimal performance.</li><li><strong>Self-healing:</strong> Automatically restarts failed containers and reschedules them if needed.</li></ol><h3>Basic Kubernetes Concepts</h3><p>To effectively use Kubernetes, it is essential to understand some basic concepts:</p><ul><li><strong>Pods:</strong> The smallest unit in Kubernetes, typically running a single instance of a container.</li><li><strong>Nodes:</strong> Machines that run containerized applications.</li><li><strong>Clusters:</strong> A set of nodes managed by Kubernetes.</li></ul>\";s:6:\"format\";s:9:\"full_html\";}}s:10:\"field_type\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:4:\"text\";}s:15:\"field_video_url\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:138:\"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Kubernetes+basics+for+ML+workloads%2C+Kubernetes+orchestration+ML%2C+Kubernetes+ML+deployment\";}s:16:\"field_video_file\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";a:3:{s:9:\"target_id\";N;s:7:\"display\";N;s:11:\"description\";N;}}s:21:\"field_zoom_meeting_id\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";N;}s:19:\"field_zoom_schedule\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";N;}s:19:\"field_scorm_package\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";a:3:{s:9:\"target_id\";N;s:7:\"display\";N;s:11:\"description\";N;}}s:14:\"field_duration\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:1:\"0\";}s:18:\"field_free_preview\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:1:\"0\";}s:15:\"field_drip_days\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:1:\"0\";}s:6:\"weight\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:1:\"0\";}s:6:\"status\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:1:\"1\";}s:7:\"created\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:10:\"1774442931\";}s:7:\"changed\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:10:\"1774519648\";}s:16:\"default_langcode\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";s:1:\"1\";}s:10:\"field_quiz\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";N;}s:21:\"field_pptx_attachment\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";a:3:{s:9:\"target_id\";N;s:7:\"display\";N;s:11:\"description\";N;}}s:14:\"field_comments\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";a:1:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"status\";s:1:\"2\";s:3:\"cid\";s:1:\"0\";s:22:\"last_comment_timestamp\";s:10:\"1774442931\";s:17:\"last_comment_name\";N;s:16:\"last_comment_uid\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"comment_count\";s:1:\"0\";}}}s:15:\"field_h5p_embed\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";N;}}s:9:\"\0*\0fields\";a: