INSERT INTO `lms_question_field_data` VALUES
(1,'single_choice','en','Which planet is known as the Red Planet?','Select the correct planet from our solar system.','full_html',10,'Mars is often called the \'Red Planet\' because of the prominent reddish color imparted by iron oxide on its surface.','full_html',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,1773833106,1773833106,1),
(2,'multiple_choice','en','Which of the following are primary colors?','Select all that apply.','full_html',10,'The primary colors are red, yellow, and blue.','full_html',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,1773833106,1773833106,1),
(3,'true_false','en','The Earth is flat.','Determine whether this statement is true or false.','full_html',5,'The Earth is an oblate spheroid, not flat.','full_html',NULL,0,0,0,0,1773833106,1773833106,1),
(4,'fill_blank','en','The capital of France is [blank_1] and the capital of Japan is [blank_2].','Fill in the correct city names for the blanks provided.','full_html',10,'Paris is the capital of France, and Tokyo is the capital of Japan.','full_html',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,1773833106,1773833106,1),
(5,'short_answer','en','What is the chemical symbol for water?','Provide the exact chemical formula.','full_html',10,'The chemical symbol for water is H2O.','full_html',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,1773833106,1773833106,1),
(6,'matching','en','Match the countries with their capitals.','Drag and drop the capital to the corresponding country.','full_html',15,'Italy -> Rome, Spain -> Madrid, Germany -> Berlin.','full_html',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,1773833106,1773833106,1),
(7,'ordering','en','Order the following historical events chronologically.','Place the earliest event at the top and the most recent at the bottom.','full_html',15,'1. Discovery of America (1492) -> 2. French Revolution (1789) -> 3. World War I (1914) -> 4. Apollo 11 Moon Landing (1969)','full_html',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,1773833106,1773833106,1),
(8,'essay','en','Explain the impact of the Industrial Revolution on modern society.','Write a short essay discussing both positive and negative impacts. Minimum 50 words.','full_html',20,'Requires manual grading by instructor based on the rubric.','full_html',NULL,NULL,0,50,500,1773833106,1773833106,1),
(9,'single_choice','en','What is the largest ocean on Earth?','Choose one option.','full_html',5,'The Pacific Ocean is the largest and deepest of Earth\'s oceanic divisions.','full_html',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,1773833106,1773833106,1),
(10,'true_false','en','Light travels faster than sound.','Is this a known scientific fact?','full_html',5,'Light travels at about 300,000 km/s, while sound travels at only 343 m/s in air.','full_html',NULL,1,0,0,0,1773833106,1773833106,1),
(11,'single_choice','en','Which keyboard key is universally used to accept an inline autocomplete suggestion from GitHub Copilot or Cursor?','Select the correct key.','full_html',10,'The \'Tab\' key is the standard shortcut to accept ghost-text inline completions generated by AI.','full_html',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,1773835308,1773835308,1),
(12,'multiple_choice','en','Which of the following are core features natively built into the Cursor IDE?','Select all that apply.','full_html',10,'Cursor includes Composer (for multi-file generation), an integrated Chat panel, and Codebase Indexing. Visual Studio Live Share is a Microsoft extension, not a native AI feature.','full_html',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,1773835308,1773835308,1),
(13,'true_false','en','GitHub Copilot can only suggest single lines of code and cannot generate entire functions.','Determine whether this statement is true or false.','full_html',5,'False. Depending on the context and the prompt (e.g., a descriptive function comment), Copilot can generate entire functions, classes, and large blocks of boilerplate code.','full_html',NULL,0,0,0,0,1773835308,1773835308,1),
(14,'fill_blank','en','Cursor IDE is an AI-first fork of the popular [blank_1] editor.','Fill in the exact name of the foundational open-source editor.','full_html',10,'Cursor is built on top of VS Code (Visual Studio Code), allowing it to support all standard VS Code extensions.','full_html',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,1773835308,1773835308,1),
(15,'short_answer','en','What does the abbreviation \'LLM\' stand for in the context of tools like Copilot and Cursor?','Provide the full phrase.','full_html',10,'LLM stands for Large Language Model, the foundational AI technology behind modern coding assistants.','full_html',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,1773835308,1773835308,1),
(16,'matching','en','Match the context symbols used in Cursor Chat with their respective functions.','Drag and drop the function to the corresponding context symbol.','full_html',15,'@Files provides context of specific files, @Codebase searches the whole workspace, and @Web does an internet lookup.','full_html',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,1773835308,1773835308,1),
(17,'ordering','en','Order the typical workflow steps for generating a new feature using Cursor Composer.','Place the first step at the top.','full_html',15,'You first open the Composer, write the prompt, let the AI generate diffs, and finally review and accept the changes.','full_html',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,1773835308,1773835308,1),
(18,'essay','en','Explain the concept of \'Context Window\' and why it is critical when using AI coding assistants.','Write a short essay (min 50 words) discussing how context limits affect code generation quality.','full_html',20,'Requires instructor review based on the student\'s understanding of token limits and context relevance.','full_html',NULL,NULL,0,50,500,1773835308,1773835308,1),
(19,'single_choice','en','When GitHub Copilot provides a suggestion you want to partially accept (word by word), which shortcut do you use?','Choose the most common shortcut for partial acceptance.','full_html',5,'Ctrl+Right Arrow (or Option/Cmd+Right Arrow on Mac) is typically used to accept suggestions word-by-word.','full_html',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,1773835308,1773835308,1),
(20,'true_false','en','You must have an active internet connection to use GitHub Copilot\'s inline autocomplete.','Is this a known requirement?','full_html',5,'True. GitHub Copilot relies on cloud-based LLMs to generate suggestions, so an internet connection is strictly required.','full_html',NULL,1,0,0,0,1773835308,1773835308,1);
